+++ b/projects/openclaw-rust/docs/specs/custody-recovery-verification.md
@@ -0,0 +1,41 @@
+# Focused custody recovery verification (CRF-v1)
+
+This is an execution selection contract inside the existing Rust desktop Actions
+workflow and portable-contract capture, not another completion ledger or runner.
+It covers the changed SC foreground producer/real consumers, repaired Plugin v3
+consumer oracles, and DJC-07's new causal COMMIT instrument. Fixed U remains
+1440bb1771372334bea23d7642bb52deb7db1845. Normal full validation remains available.
+
+- **CRF-01:** The explicit custody-recovery scope runs only on the exact checked-out
+  full H/tree with locked dependencies, bound source bytes, command/capture exits,
+  raw logs and artifact identities. Reject an unknown scope or moved dispatch ref.
+  Reuse the existing workflow, Rust toolchain/cache and portable capture.
+- **CRF-02:** Select the existing eleven Box response/capture command groups,
+  retaining their complete named positives, normal daemon build and separately
+  qualified fault-test artifact; select each of the three repaired desktop tests
+  exactly and the existing library handoff test; select the new DJC-07 test exactly.
+  Derive reused commands and requirements from the existing full plan and require
+  unique, nonempty labels/names. The full plan still requires all old tests.
+- **CRF-03:** A selected single-target check requires exactly the declared positive
+  names once, one successful nonempty libtest summary, zero failed/ignored/measured,
+  and successful command and capture exits. Filtered tests are permitted only for
+  explicitly selected filtered commands. Preserve existing artifact/oracle controls
+  and add scope/selection and selected-result negatives. Never treat absent checks
+  or synthetic oracle controls as product positives.
+- **CRF-04:** Run the selected Rust checks and shipping Host compile on Linux and
+  macOS. Existing unrelated Windows/media/renderer/config jobs are not part of this
+  explicitly selected recovery; their prior evidence remains separate. Normal full
+  and existing scopes retain their original jobs. No local/htch execution is allowed.
+- **CRF-05:** The capture marks a successful selected receipt as scoped-only, records
+  the selected plan and unexecuted full-plan cases, and makes no full-contract/global
+  acceptance claim. Palette export is required whenever its producing case is
+  selected; do not claim an export for this selection. Source/binary/lock stability
+  remains mandatory for the actually executed producer and consumer boundaries.
+- **CRF-06:** Preserve the historical DJC reader-lock eight-second failure and its
+  unchanged source assertion. It is not rerun by this focused selection and remains
+  unresolved, even if DJC-07 passes. This selection follows the independent directness
+  assessment; it cannot serve as a third identical lock campaign or erase past failure.
+- **CRF-07:** Review the full changed workflow/capture/test surface before execution.
+  Missing/extra/duplicate names, bad summaries, wrong scope, missing selected commands,
+  changed sources, failed builds and unbound artifacts must fail. Keep production
+  owner/state/schema, OCRM inventory/ledger/RTM and all global completion flags intact.
diff --git a/projects/openclaw-rust/docs/specs/device-pairing-join-admission.md b/projects/openclaw-rust/docs/specs/device-pairing-join-admission.md
